9) by its keys"] [828 3 "// PyMapping_Keys: an exact dict's keys, any other mapping's keys() (a dict subclass's own too; py-core-1124:"] [829 3 "// test_builtin's test_general_eval)"] [833 4 "// PyMapping_Keys"] [886 2 "// the readline module imported and both streams the process's terminals (builtin_input's tty path over"] [887 2 "// PyOS_Readline, queue 289): the line by its editor, the prompt its own"] [916 2 "// builtin_input_impl: sys.stdout flushed before the read (queue 551: a real TextIOWrapper's flush too)"] [924 3 "// the fallback's _PyFile_Flush: an error cleared (py-core-1124: test_builtin's test_input, a stdout with no flush)"] [959 1 "// intRound is int.__round__ (long_round): ndigits by __index__ (a TypeError for others), an exact int of the value"] [960 1 "// when it is not negative, else the value rounded half-even to 10**-ndigits (_PyLong_DivmodNear) at any size (queue"] [961 1 "// 328: it was int64's, so a big int or a big ndigits went wrong: test_long's test_round)."] [975 2 "// 10**k past twice |v|: the nearest multiple is 0 (10**k has k+1 digits)"] [980 50 "// Euclidean: 0 <= r < p"] [988 1 "// roundFloat is float.__round__ (Objects/floatobject.c's double_round): to an int, ties to even, without"] [989 1 "// ndigits; else the correctly rounded value at ndigits decimal places (round-half-even on the exact decimal"] [990 1 "// value, as dtoa's mode 3), negative ndigits rounding to tens, hundreds ..."] [1002 2 "// PyNumber_AsSsize_t(o_ndigits, NULL): an ndigits past ssize_t clamped (queue 328: test_float's test_large_n)"] [1019 2 "// the exact decimal value of x, rounded half-even at n places after the point"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[20 48] [26 49] [40 47] [58 46] [64 48] [74 52] [89 41] [99 48] [108 41] [121 41] [137 52] [140 32] [146 51] [186 31] [219 31] [224 39] [232 28] [236 37] [245 37] [253 43] [257 35] [262 32] [273 35] [300 46] [304 22] [314 28] [317 43] [347 34] [367 44] [422 45] [445 43] [459 43] [473 46] [490 